Spring Cloud Sleuth automatically instruments Spring Boot applications for tracing. Implementation:

pom.xml:
<dependency>
  <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>
  <artifactId>spring-cloud-starter-sleuth</artifactId>
</dependency>
<dependency>
  <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>
  <artifactId>spring-cloud-sleuth-zipkin</artifactId>
</dependency>

application.yml:
spring:
  sleuth:
    sampler:
      probability: 0.1  # Sample 10% of traces
  zipkin:
    base-url: http://zipkin:9411
    sender:
      type: web

Sleuth automatically:
- Adds trace/span IDs to logs: [payment-service,abc123,xyz789]
- Propagates IDs via HTTP headers
- Instruments RestTemplate, WebClient, messaging

Custom spans:
@Service
public class PaymentService {
  @Autowired
  private Tracer tracer;

  public Payment processPayment(PaymentRequest request) {
    Span span = tracer.nextSpan().name("process-payment");
    try (Tracer.SpanInScope ws = tracer.withSpanInScope(span.start())) {
      span.tag("payment.amount", request.getAmount().toString());
      span.tag("payment.provider", request.getProvider());

      Payment payment = callPaymentGateway(request);

      span.event("payment-processed");
      return payment;
    } catch (Exception e) {
      span.error(e);
      throw e;
    } finally {
      span.finish();
    }
  }
}

Traces sent to Zipkin, visualize in UI: service dependencies graph, trace timeline, span details.

OpenTelemetry (OTel) is vendor-neutral observability framework (CNCF project). Provides unified APIs and SDKs for traces, metrics, logs. Differences from proprietary: 1) Vendor-agnostic - switch backends without code changes, 2) Open standard - wide tool support, 3) Unified - single SDK for all telemetry, 4) Community-driven. Architecture: Application uses OTel SDK → Exports to OTel Collector → Backends (Jaeger, Prometheus, etc.). Implementation:

pom.xml:
<dependency>
  <groupId>io.opentelemetry</groupId>
  <artifactId>opentelemetry-api</artifactId>
</dependency>
<dependency>
  <groupId>io.opentelemetry.instrumentation</groupId>
  <artifactId>opentelemetry-spring-boot-starter</artifactId>
</dependency>

application.yml:
otel:
  traces:
    exporter: otlp
  exporter:
    otlp:
      endpoint: http://otel-collector:4317
  resource:
    attributes:
      service.name: payment-service
      deployment.environment: production

Manual instrumentation:
@Service
public class PaymentService {
  private final Tracer tracer;

  public PaymentService(OpenTelemetry openTelemetry) {
    this.tracer = openTelemetry.getTracer("payment-service");
  }

  public Payment processPayment(PaymentRequest request) {
    Span span = tracer.spanBuilder("processPayment")
      .setSpanKind(SpanKind.INTERNAL)
      .startSpan();

    try (Scope scope = span.makeCurrent()) {
      span.setAttribute("payment.amount", request.getAmount());
      span.addEvent("Payment processing started");

      Payment payment = gateway.process(request);

      span.setStatus(StatusCode.OK);
      return payment;
    } catch (Exception e) {
      span.recordException(e);
      span.setStatus(StatusCode.ERROR);
      throw e;
    } finally {
      span.end();
    }
  }
}

Benefits: future-proof (no vendor lock-in), consistent telemetry, growing ecosystem. Adoption: Google, Microsoft, Datadog, New Relic support OTel.
